GDN prefill checkpoints: wire the Qwen GDN path into the
backend-neutral prefill checkpoint machinery. Default off
(VLLM_GDN_PREFILL_CHECKPOINTS); no behavior change when unset.

Qwen GDN (Gated DeltaNet) layers build their MambaSpec from the
shared base get_kv_cache_spec, which never sets
num_prefill_checkpoint_blocks, so the prefill checkpoint machinery
(MambaPrefillCheckpointBuilder, the manager's per-request
checkpoint block, MambaPrefillCheckpointMetadata) stays permanently
dormant for GDN models on every vLLM release through 0.32. Mamba2
and KDA both opt in; GDN never does.

  - QwenGatedDeltaNetAttention.get_kv_cache_spec sets
    num_prefill_checkpoint_blocks=1, prefill_checkpoint_alignment=1
    when the gate is set (one dedicated state block per request,
    already accounted for by MambaSpec.max_memory_usage).
  - GDNAttentionMetadataBuilder instantiates the builder and
    resolves per-batch checkpoint rows in build() (align mode only;
    the same contract KDA/Mamba2 use).
  - The GDN prefill path exports the checkpoint when it lands on a
    row end: the chunk kernel (fla/flashinfer) returns exactly one
    final state per row, so a mid-query checkpoint cannot be
    exported from the row final state. Those rows decline (their
    allocated block stays null) rather than being written from a
    different state. The conv portion of the checkpoint block is
    zero-filled (deterministic; perturbs at most the first
    conv_kernel_size - 1 resumed positions).

Why row-end only: the stock validity rules (hash-aligned row start,
position strictly interior) rarely hold for 1024-token chunked
prefill steps under a 2048 hash grid with the EAGLE margin dropped,
and when they do, the position is interior to the row. Full
mid-prefill GDN checkpoints need either per-chunk state output from
the GDN kernel or a GDN-scoped position grid in the manager; this
patch sets up that follow-up rather than doing it.

Written against vLLM 0.31.0.

Kind: feature
What: GDN prefill checkpoint plumbing (spec opt-in + GDN metadata wiring + row-end writer), gated on VLLM_GDN_PREFILL_CHECKPOINTS (default off)
Upstream: not present in 0.31/0.32 for GDN; machinery = vllm mamba/checkpoint.py + MambaSpec.num_prefill_checkpoint_blocks (cf. Mamba2/KDA opt-in in 0.32)
Cut-against: 0.31.0
Retires-when: GDN prefill checkpoints land upstream, or a GDN-scoped position grid supersedes the stock validity rules

